# C09 message page actions — unapplied attach

Issue: https://github.com/liboyang42-cpu/chengyin-remote-ops/issues/5
Repo: github.com/liboyang42-cpu/chengyin-ios
Base: origin/cursor/c09-message-page-actions-e504 `e393b9b39ec1d1988117d9e18f69d5d1e6fa6ca6`

`NativeChannelMessagePageActions` forwards the normal channel message page.
Send calls `NativeChannelTextCoordinator.sendNew(_:)` once.
Edit, recall, and pin each call `NativeChannelMessageCoordinator.submit(_:)` once.
The synchronous throws-to-dictionary port is not the writer.
The same request is read back with the original journal `restore`.
A different request, a blank body, or a missing proof stays UNKNOWN and does not clear the journal.
A sparse submitted receipt with `message_unavailable` and no MessagingMessage is not rejected.
This file does not fabricate a MessagingMessage, rewrite a request id, or add a receipt store.
`appear()` does not send. Search stays on `NativeChannelMessageEntry`.
Do not block `sendNew` or `submit` with a synchronous wrapper. The original methods are already async.
Do not call `ImmutableReceiptProducer.accept` or `recoverOriginal`.

Do not apply this hunk onto `App/MessagingHistoryView.swift`, `App/AppSession.swift`, `App/AppCompositionRoot.swift`, or `Questify.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj`. Those files stay unchanged. Do not edit journal persist, restore, or settle. The SwiftUI page below is also not applied.

XCTest NOT_RUN where swiftc is absent. Not 100%.

## Original command conformance (not applied)

```
extension NativeChannelTextCoordinator: NativeChannelOriginalTextCommand {}
extension NativeChannelMessageCoordinator: NativeChannelOriginalMessageCommand {}
extension NativeChannelTextJournal: NativeChannelOriginalTextJournal {}
extension NativeChannelMessageMutationJournal: NativeChannelOriginalMutationJournal {}
extension NativeChannelMessageCommand: NativeChannelOriginalMutationIdentity {}
```

`NativeChannelTextCoordinator.sendNew(_:)` and `NativeChannelMessageCoordinator.submit(_:)` stay the original methods.
`NativeChannelTextJournal.restore()` and `NativeChannelMessageMutationJournal.restore()` stay the original reads.
Do not add a second journal or a second search chain.

## Page patch (not applied)

Existing page: `App/MessagingHistoryView.swift`. No gradient, glow, or emoji icons. The resting layout is unchanged. Appearance calls `appear()` only. `channelActions` is optional until the existing host supplies the original coordinators. A nil page does not send.

```
diff --git a/App/MessagingHistoryView.swift b/App/MessagingHistoryView.swift
--- a/App/MessagingHistoryView.swift
+++ b/App/MessagingHistoryView.swift
@@ -62,6 +62,7 @@ struct MessagingHistoryView: View {
     @State private var generation: UInt64 = 0
     @State private var visibleMessageID: Int?
     @State private var showingPollComposer = false
+    @State private var channelActions: ChannelPageActions?

     init(conversationID: Int, conversation: MessagingConversation? = nil, reader: any MessagingReading, sender:MessageActionCoordinator?=nil,mediaReader:(any SocialMessageMediaReading)?=nil,expanded:IMExpandedNavigationContext?=nil, onConversationMutationAccepted: @escaping (IMScope) -> Void = { _ in }) {
@@ -159,6 +160,7 @@ struct MessagingHistoryView: View {
             // Only a new account epoch or an unfinished first load starts an automatic read.
             if !currentHistoryReady { await reload() }
         }
+        .onAppear { channelActions?.appear() }
         .onDisappear { generation &+= 1; isLoadingEarlier = false }
     }
@@ -247,6 +249,28 @@ struct MessagingHistoryView: View {
             && ObjectIdentifier(reader) == source && reader.isConfigured
             && history.conversationID == conversationID
     }
+    func sendChannel(requestID: String?, content: String?) async throws -> NativeChannelOriginalRead {
+        guard let channelActions else { throw NotifyFailure.waitingSource(capability: "native-channel-text.sendNew") }
+        return try await channelActions.send(requestID: requestID, content: content)
+    }
+    func editChannel(command: NativeChannelMessageCommand) async throws -> NativeChannelOriginalRead {
+        guard let channelActions else { throw NotifyFailure.waitingSource(capability: "native-channel-message.submit") }
+        return try await channelActions.edit(command: command)
+    }
+    func recallChannel(command: NativeChannelMessageCommand) async throws -> NativeChannelOriginalRead {
+        guard let channelActions else { throw NotifyFailure.waitingSource(capability: "native-channel-message.submit") }
+        return try await channelActions.recall(command: command)
+    }
+    func pinChannel(command: NativeChannelMessageCommand) async throws -> NativeChannelOriginalRead {
+        guard let channelActions else { throw NotifyFailure.waitingSource(capability: "native-channel-message.submit") }
+        return try await channelActions.pin(command: command)
+    }
 }
+typealias ChannelPageActions = NativeChannelMessagePageActions<
+    NativeChannelTextCoordinator,
+    NativeChannelMessageCoordinator,
+    NativeChannelTextJournal,
+    NativeChannelMessageMutationJournal>
```

`channelActions.send(`, `channelActions.edit(`, `channelActions.recall(`, `channelActions.pin(` each run once per page call.
Send reaches `textCoordinator.sendNew` once. Edit, recall, and pin each reach `messageCoordinator.submit` once.
`channelActions.appear()` does not send.
`channelActions?.appear()` does not send when the page is absent.

